        val subtitles = listOf(
            VodSubtitle("https://x/en.srt", "en", "English", "application/x-subrip"),
            VodSubtitle("https://x/pt.srt", "pt-BR", "Português", "application/x-subrip")
        )
        assertEquals(
            "pt-BR",
            VodSubtitleSupport.preferPortuguese(subtitles).first().language
        )
    }

    @Test
    fun buildsCommonsTimedTextVttUrl() {
        val url = WikimediaSubtitleSupport.timedTextUrl(
            "File:Krazy Kat Bugologist 1916 silent.ogv",
            "pt-br"
        )
        assertTrue(url.startsWith("https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/api.php"))
        assertTrue(url.contains("action=timedtext"))
        assertTrue(url.contains("trackformat=vtt"))
        assertTrue(url.contains("lang=pt-br"))
    }

    @Test
    fun detectsWebVttPayload() {
        assertTrue(
            WikimediaSubtitleSupport.looksLikeSubtitle(
                "WEBVTT\n\n00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:03.000\nOlá"
            )
        )
    }

    @Test
    fun rightsPolicyAcceptsPublicDomainAndCreativeCommons() {
        assertTrue(ArchiveRightsPolicy.isOpen("Public Domain", null))
        assertTrue(
            ArchiveRightsPolicy.isOpen(
                null,
                "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"
            )
        )
    }
}

# SANCHESTV 2.8

**Instalar → abrir → assistir.**

SANCHESTV é uma central Android TV / Google TV com IPTV, EPG e agora uma área de cinema VOD multi-fonte. O package `com.mukasanches.zapptv` e a assinatura oficial iniciada na 2.7 permanecem estáveis para permitir atualização por cima da release anterior.

## Destaques 2.8 — Cinema Livre

- nova área **Cinema** com catálogo VOD real, independente dos canais lineares;
- catálogo remoto paginado: o APK não carrega uma lista fixa e pode buscar novas páginas continuamente;
- **23 catálogos lógicos públicos/licenciados**:
  - 8 recortes do Internet Archive, incluindo Open Source Movies, Prelinger e gêneros com verificação de licença/direitos;
  - 6 recortes de vídeo do Wikimedia Commons: filmes, cinema mudo, animação, documentários, curtas e cinema;
  - 8 coleções cinematográficas da Library of Congress;
  - Blender Foundation • Open Movies;
- deduplicação por título normalizado + ano para reduzir cópias do mesmo filme;
- pesquisa local por título, descrição, gênero, ano, fonte e catálogo;
- filtros por catálogo;
- resolução sob demanda do arquivo reproduzível do Internet Archive;
- player VOD Media3 separado do player de TV ao vivo;
- suporte a legendas externas **SubRip/SRT, WebVTT e TTML**;
- descoberta automática de TimedText do Wikimedia Commons em **pt-BR, pt, en e es**;
- preferência automática por **pt-BR → pt → en → es**;
- botão de legenda percorre as faixas reais encontradas e permite desligar;
- faixas de legenda embutidas do próprio HLS/DASH continuam funcionando;
- **Tears of Steel** incluído como Open Movie de referência de reprodução;
- proveniência, licença/rights e fonte preservadas no modelo do item;
- cache HTTP de catálogo para reduzir recarregamentos;
- base IPTV 2.7 preservada: M3U Watcher, EPG multi-dia, Turbo Preload, diagnóstico e atualizador SHA-256.

## Fontes e direitos

O cinema da 2.8 foi desenhado para fontes públicas, livres ou disponibilizadas oficialmente para visualização. O app não inclui DRM bypass, scraping de serviços fechados, credenciais de terceiros, tokens privados ou catálogos piratas.

O SANCHESTV mantém o nome da fonte e os campos de licença/direitos quando disponíveis. Para o Internet Archive, o arquivo reproduzível e as legendas são descobertos no registro do próprio item. No Wikimedia Commons são lidos metadados de licença do arquivo. Na Library of Congress o app preserva o registro de direitos da National Screening Room.

## Legendas

O player VOD usa `MediaItem.SubtitleConfiguration` do AndroidX Media3 para sideload de legendas externas. Para vídeos do Commons, a 2.8 consulta a API oficial TimedText e adiciona as faixas disponíveis ao player. Formatos aceitos pelo adaptador da 2.8:

- `.srt` → `application/x-subrip`;
- `.vtt` → `text/vtt`;
- `.ttml` → `application/ttml+xml`.

Quando existem várias faixas, PT-BR recebe prioridade. O controle de legenda percorre as faixas encontradas, inclui modo desligado e mantém suporte às faixas embutidas do próprio vídeo.

## Arquitetura

```text
IPTV / M3U / XMLTV                     CINEMA VOD
        │                                  │
M3U Watcher + EPG                 IA / Commons / LOC / Open Movies
        │                                  │
Channel Graph                     paginação + dedupe + proveniência
        │                                  │
Media3 Live Player                resolução de mídia + legendas
        └──────────────┬───────────────────┘
                       │
                  SANCHESTV UI
```

## Build

Toolchain validada:

- JDK 17
- Android compileSdk 36
- minSdk 26
- targetSdk 35
- Gradle 8.13
- Kotlin 2.3.21
- Media3 1.11.1

Validação:

```bash
gradle --no-daemon testDebugUnitTest
gradle --no-daemon lintDebug
gradle --no-daemon assembleRelease
```

A release oficial usa a mesma chave protegida da SANCHESTV 2.7. O keystore e as senhas não ficam no repositório.

O pipeline oficial verifica:

- package `com.mukasanches.zapptv`;
- versionCode 12;
- versionName 2.8.0;
- APK não debuggable;
- R8/shrink de recursos;
- assinatura com `apksigner verify`;
- SHA-256 do APK;
- fingerprint SHA-256 do certificado.

## Privacidade

Favoritos, histórico, ranking de canais e preferências continuam no dispositivo. O catálogo de cinema é consultado diretamente nas fontes públicas e não exige conta SANCHESTV.

package com.mukasanches.zapptv.vod

import java.text.Normalizer
import kotlin.math.abs

object CinemaRightsEngine {
    fun classify(
        source: String,
        licenseName: String?,
        licenseUrl: String?
    ): RightsStatus {
        val text = listOfNotNull(source, licenseName, licenseUrl)
            .joinToString(" ")
            .lowercase()

        return when {
            "public domain" in text ||
                "publicdomain" in text ||
                "no known copyright" in text ||
                "no known restrictions" in text -> RightsStatus.PUBLIC_DOMAIN

            "creativecommons.org/publicdomain" in text ||
                "cc0" in text -> RightsStatus.PUBLIC_DOMAIN

            "cc-by-sa" in text ||
                "cc by-sa" in text ||
                "by-sa" in text -> RightsStatus.ATTRIBUTION_REQUIRED

            "cc-by" in text ||
                "cc by" in text ||
                "creative commons attribution" in text -> RightsStatus.ATTRIBUTION_REQUIRED

            "creativecommons.org" in text ||
                "creative commons" in text -> RightsStatus.OPEN_LICENSE

            source.equals("Wikimedia Commons", ignoreCase = true) ->
                RightsStatus.OPEN_LICENSE

            source.startsWith("NASA", ignoreCase = true) ->
                RightsStatus.OPEN_LICENSE

            "all rights reserved" in text ||
                "restricted" in text -> RightsStatus.RESTRICTED

            else -> RightsStatus.UNKNOWN
        }
    }

    fun normalize(item: VodItem): VodItem {
        val status = if (item.rightsStatus == RightsStatus.UNKNOWN) {
            classify(item.source, item.licenseName, item.licenseUrl)
        } else {
            item.rightsStatus
        }
        return item.copy(
            rightsStatus = status,
            providers = (item.providers + item.source)
                .filter(String::isNotBlank)
                .distinct()
        )
    }

    fun canAutoPlay(item: VodItem): Boolean =
        item.rightsStatus in setOf(
            RightsStatus.PUBLIC_DOMAIN,
            RightsStatus.OPEN_LICENSE,
            RightsStatus.ATTRIBUTION_REQUIRED
        ) || item.source == "Wikimedia Commons" ||
            item.source.startsWith("NASA", ignoreCase = true)
}

object MovieIdentityResolver {
    fun merge(items: List<VodItem>): List<VodItem> {
        val result = mutableListOf<VodItem>()

        items.map(CinemaRightsEngine::normalize).forEach { incoming ->
            val matchIndex = result.indexOfFirst { existing ->
                sameMovie(existing, incoming)
            }

            if (matchIndex < 0) {
                result += incoming
            } else {
                result[matchIndex] = mergePair(result[matchIndex], incoming)
            }
        }

        return result.sortedWith(
            compareByDescending<VodItem> { it.playable }
                .thenByDescending { it.subtitles.any { sub -> sub.language.startsWith("pt") } }
                .thenBy { it.title.lowercase() }
        )
    }

    fun identityKey(item: VodItem): String {
        val title = normalizeTitle(item.title)
        val year = item.year?.take(4).orEmpty()
        return if (year.isBlank()) title else "$title|$year"
    }

    internal fun sameMovie(a: VodItem, b: VodItem): Boolean {
        val titleA = normalizeTitle(a.title)
        val titleB = normalizeTitle(b.title)
        if (titleA == titleB) {
            val yearA = a.year?.take(4)?.toIntOrNull()
            val yearB = b.year?.take(4)?.toIntOrNull()
            return yearA == null || yearB == null || abs(yearA - yearB) <= 1
        }

        if (titleA.length < 6 || titleB.length < 6) return false
        val tokensA = titleA.split(' ').filter { it.length > 2 }.toSet()
        val tokensB = titleB.split(' ').filter { it.length > 2 }.toSet()
        if (tokensA.isEmpty() || tokensB.isEmpty()) return false
        val intersection = tokensA.intersect(tokensB).size.toDouble()
        val union = tokensA.union(tokensB).size.toDouble()
        val similarity = if (union == 0.0) 0.0 else intersection / union
        if (similarity < 0.88) return false

        val yearA = a.year?.take(4)?.toIntOrNull()
        val yearB = b.year?.take(4)?.toIntOrNull()
        return yearA == null || yearB == null || abs(yearA - yearB) <= 1
    }

    private fun mergePair(a: VodItem, b: VodItem): VodItem {
        val primary = choosePrimary(a, b)
        val secondary = if (primary === a) b else a

        val allPlayback = buildList {
            primary.playbackUrl?.let(::add)
            secondary.playbackUrl?.let(::add)
            addAll(primary.alternatePlaybackUrls)
            addAll(secondary.alternatePlaybackUrls)
        }.filter(String::isNotBlank).distinct()

        return primary.copy(
            overview = primary.overview.ifBlank { secondary.overview },
            posterUrl = primary.posterUrl ?: secondary.posterUrl,
            backdropUrl = primary.backdropUrl ?: secondary.backdropUrl,
            year = primary.year ?: secondary.year,
            genres = (primary.genres + secondary.genres).distinct().take(12),
            language = primary.language.takeUnless { it == "und" } ?: secondary.language,
            playbackUrl = allPlayback.firstOrNull(),
            licenseName = primary.licenseName ?: secondary.licenseName,
            licenseUrl = primary.licenseUrl ?: secondary.licenseUrl,
            attribution = primary.attribution ?: secondary.attribution,
            subtitles = VodSubtitleSupport.preferPortuguese(
                primary.subtitles + secondary.subtitles
            ),
            rightsStatus = strongerRights(primary.rightsStatus, secondary.rightsStatus),
            providers = (primary.providers + secondary.providers + primary.source + secondary.source)
                .filter(String::isNotBlank)
                .distinct(),
            alternatePlaybackUrls = allPlayback.drop(1),
            externalIds = primary.externalIds + secondary.externalIds,
            durationSeconds = primary.durationSeconds ?: secondary.durationSeconds
        )
    }

    private fun choosePrimary(a: VodItem, b: VodItem): VodItem =
        listOf(a, b).maxByOrNull { item ->
            var score = 0
            if (item.playable) score += 100
            if (item.subtitles.any { it.language == "pt-BR" }) score += 30
            if (item.posterUrl != null) score += 10
            if (item.overview.isNotBlank()) score += 5
            score += when (item.rightsStatus) {
                RightsStatus.PUBLIC_DOMAIN -> 20
                RightsStatus.OPEN_LICENSE -> 18
                RightsStatus.ATTRIBUTION_REQUIRED -> 16
                RightsStatus.UNKNOWN -> 0
                RightsStatus.RESTRICTED -> -100
            }
            score
        } ?: a

    private fun strongerRights(a: RightsStatus, b: RightsStatus): RightsStatus {
        val rank = mapOf(
            RightsStatus.PUBLIC_DOMAIN to 5,
            RightsStatus.OPEN_LICENSE to 4,
            RightsStatus.ATTRIBUTION_REQUIRED to 3,
            RightsStatus.UNKNOWN to 2,
            RightsStatus.RESTRICTED to 1
        )
        return if ((rank[a] ?: 0) >= (rank[b] ?: 0)) a else b
    }

    internal fun normalizeTitle(value: String): String =
        Normalizer.normalize(value, Normalizer.Form.NFD)
            .replace(Regex("\\p{M}+"), "")
            .uppercase()
            .replace(Regex("[^A-Z0-9]+"), " ")
            .replace(Regex("\\b(THE|A|AN|O|A|OS|AS|UM|UMA|DE|DA|DO|DAS|DOS)\\b"), " ")
            .replace(Regex("\\s+"), " ")
            .trim()
}

package com.mukasanches.zapptv.vod

import android.content.ContentValues
import android.content.Context
import android.database.sqlite.SQLiteDatabase
import android.database.sqlite.SQLiteOpenHelper
import org.json.JSONArray
import org.json.JSONObject

data class CinemaIndexStats(
    val indexed: Int = 0,
    val playable: Int = 0,
    val portugueseSubtitles: Int = 0
)

class CinemaIndexStore(context: Context) :
    SQLiteOpenHelper(context.applicationContext, DB_NAME, null, DB_VERSION) {

    override fun onCreate(db: SQLiteDatabase) {
        db.execSQL(
            """
            CREATE TABLE $TABLE_MOVIES (
                identity_key TEXT PRIMARY KEY NOT NULL,
                item_json TEXT NOT NULL,
                search_text TEXT NOT NULL,
                playable INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,
                has_pt_sub INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,
                updated_at INTEGER NOT NULL
            )
            """.trimIndent()
        )
        db.execSQL("CREATE INDEX idx_movie_updated ON $TABLE_MOVIES(updated_at DESC)")
        db.execSQL("CREATE INDEX idx_movie_playable ON $TABLE_MOVIES(playable, updated_at DESC)")
    }

    override fun onUpgrade(db: SQLiteDatabase, oldVersion: Int, newVersion: Int) {
        if (oldVersion != newVersion) {
            db.execSQL("DROP TABLE IF EXISTS $TABLE_MOVIES")
            onCreate(db)
        }
    }

    fun upsert(items: List<VodItem>) {
        if (items.isEmpty()) return
        val now = System.currentTimeMillis()
        writableDatabase.beginTransaction()
        try {
            items.forEach { item ->
                val normalized = CinemaRightsEngine.normalize(item)
                val key = MovieIdentityResolver.identityKey(normalized)
                if (key.isBlank()) return@forEach

                val values = ContentValues().apply {
                    put("identity_key", key)
                    put("item_json", toJson(normalized).toString())
                    put("search_text", searchText(normalized))
                    put("playable", if (normalized.playable) 1 else 0)
                    put(
                        "has_pt_sub",
                        if (normalized.subtitles.any { it.language.startsWith("pt") }) 1 else 0
                    )
                    put("updated_at", now)
                }
                writableDatabase.insertWithOnConflict(
                    TABLE_MOVIES,
                    null,
                    values,
                    SQLiteDatabase.CONFLICT_REPLACE
                )
            }
            writableDatabase.setTransactionSuccessful()
        } finally {
            writableDatabase.endTransaction()
        }
    }

    fun search(query: String, limit: Int = 250): List<VodItem> {
        val q = query.trim()
        if (q.isBlank()) return recent(limit)

        val like = "%${escapeLike(normalizeSearch(q))}%"
        val cursor = readableDatabase.query(
            TABLE_MOVIES,
            arrayOf("item_json"),
            "search_text LIKE ? ESCAPE '\\'",
            arrayOf(like),
            null,
            null,
            "playable DESC, has_pt_sub DESC, updated_at DESC",
            limit.coerceIn(1, 1000).toString()
        )

        return cursor.use {
            buildList {
                while (it.moveToNext()) {
                    fromJson(it.getString(0))?.let(::add)
                }
            }
        }
    }

    fun recent(limit: Int = 250): List<VodItem> {
        val cursor = readableDatabase.query(
            TABLE_MOVIES,
            arrayOf("item_json"),
            null,
            null,
            null,
            null,
            "updated_at DESC",
            limit.coerceIn(1, 1000).toString()
        )

        return cursor.use {
            buildList {
                while (it.moveToNext()) {
                    fromJson(it.getString(0))?.let(::add)
                }
            }
        }
    }

    fun stats(): CinemaIndexStats {
        val cursor = readableDatabase.rawQuery(
            """
            SELECT
                COUNT(*),
                SUM(CASE WHEN playable = 1 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END),
                SUM(CASE WHEN has_pt_sub = 1 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END)
            FROM $TABLE_MOVIES
            """.trimIndent(),
            null
        )
        return cursor.use {
            if (!it.moveToFirst()) return@use CinemaIndexStats()
            CinemaIndexStats(
                indexed = it.getInt(0),
                playable = if (it.isNull(1)) 0 else it.getInt(1),
                portugueseSubtitles = if (it.isNull(2)) 0 else it.getInt(2)
            )
        }
    }

    private fun searchText(item: VodItem): String =
        normalizeSearch(
            listOf(
                item.title,
                item.overview,
                item.year.orEmpty(),
                item.source,
                item.catalog,
                item.genres.joinToString(" "),
                item.providers.joinToString(" "),
                item.attribution.orEmpty()
            ).joinToString(" ")
        )

    private fun normalizeSearch(value: String): String =
        MovieIdentityResolver.normalizeTitle(value).lowercase()

    private fun escapeLike(value: String): String =
        value.replace("\\", "\\\\")
            .replace("%", "\\%")
            .replace("_", "\\_")

    private fun toJson(item: VodItem): JSONObject =
        JSONObject().apply {
            put("id", item.id)
            put("title", item.title)
            put("overview", item.overview)
            put("posterUrl", item.posterUrl)
            put("backdropUrl", item.backdropUrl)
            put("year", item.year)
            put("genres", JSONArray(item.genres))
            put("language", item.language)
            put("playbackUrl", item.playbackUrl)
            put("source", item.source)
            put("catalog", item.catalog)
            put("detailUrl", item.detailUrl)
            put("licenseName", item.licenseName)
            put("licenseUrl", item.licenseUrl)
            put("attribution", item.attribution)
            put("subtitleLookupKey", item.subtitleLookupKey)
            put("rightsStatus", item.rightsStatus.name)
            put("providers", JSONArray(item.providers))
            put("alternatePlaybackUrls", JSONArray(item.alternatePlaybackUrls))
            put("durationSeconds", item.durationSeconds)
            put("kind", item.kind.name)

            val ids = JSONObject()
            item.externalIds.forEach(ids::put)
            put("externalIds", ids)

            val subtitles = JSONArray()
            item.subtitles.forEach { subtitle ->
                subtitles.put(
                    JSONObject().apply {
                        put("uri", subtitle.uri)
                        put("language", subtitle.language)
                        put("label", subtitle.label)
                        put("mimeType", subtitle.mimeType)
                        put("isDefault", subtitle.isDefault)
                    }
                )
            }
            put("subtitles", subtitles)
        }

    private fun fromJson(value: String): VodItem? =
        runCatching {
            val json = JSONObject(value)
            val subtitlesJson = json.optJSONArray("subtitles") ?: JSONArray()
            val subtitles = buildList {
                for (i in 0 until subtitlesJson.length()) {
                    val sub = subtitlesJson.optJSONObject(i) ?: continue
                    add(
                        VodSubtitle(
                            uri = sub.optString("uri"),
                            language = sub.optString("language", "und"),
                            label = sub.optString("label", "Legenda"),
                            mimeType = sub.optString("mimeType"),
                            isDefault = sub.optBoolean("isDefault", false)
                        )
                    )
                }
            }

            val idsJson = json.optJSONObject("externalIds") ?: JSONObject()
            val ids = buildMap {
                idsJson.keys().forEach { key ->
                    put(key, idsJson.optString(key))
                }
            }

            VodItem(
                id = json.getString("id"),
                title = json.getString("title"),
                overview = json.optString("overview"),
                posterUrl = json.optString("posterUrl").takeIf(String::isNotBlank),
                backdropUrl = json.optString("backdropUrl").takeIf(String::isNotBlank),
                year = json.optString("year").takeIf(String::isNotBlank),
                genres = json.optJSONArray("genres").toStringList(),
                language = json.optString("language", "und"),
                playbackUrl = json.optString("playbackUrl").takeIf(String::isNotBlank),
                source = json.optString("source"),
                catalog = json.optString("catalog"),
                detailUrl = json.optString("detailUrl").takeIf(String::isNotBlank),
                licenseName = json.optString("licenseName").takeIf(String::isNotBlank),
                licenseUrl = json.optString("licenseUrl").takeIf(String::isNotBlank),
                attribution = json.optString("attribution").takeIf(String::isNotBlank),
                subtitleLookupKey = json.optString("subtitleLookupKey").takeIf(String::isNotBlank),
                subtitles = subtitles,
                rightsStatus = runCatching {
                    RightsStatus.valueOf(json.optString("rightsStatus"))
                }.getOrDefault(RightsStatus.UNKNOWN),
                providers = json.optJSONArray("providers").toStringList(),
                alternatePlaybackUrls = json.optJSONArray("alternatePlaybackUrls").toStringList(),
                externalIds = ids,
                durationSeconds = json.optLong("durationSeconds").takeIf { it > 0L },
                kind = runCatching {
                    VodItem.Kind.valueOf(json.optString("kind"))
                }.getOrDefault(VodItem.Kind.MOVIE)
            )
        }.getOrNull()

    private fun JSONArray?.toStringList(): List<String> {
        if (this == null) return emptyList()
        return buildList {
            for (i in 0 until length()) {
                optString(i).takeIf(String::isNotBlank)?.let(::add)
            }
        }
    }

    companion object {
        private const val DB_NAME = "sanchestv-cinema-index.db"
        private const val DB_VERSION = 1
        private const val TABLE_MOVIES = "movie_index"
    }
}

package com.mukasanches.zapptv.vod

